  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> Ammonia is strong field ligand and electronic configuration of </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hybridisation: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>Pairing of electrons takes place due to the strong field ligand. Hence, it is inner orbital complex (spin paired complex).</p><p>In the complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>CoF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> fluoride is weak field ligand and electronic configuration of  <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Hybridisation: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Pairing of electrons not takes place due to the weak field ligand. Hence, it is outer orbital complex (spin free complex).</p><p>Hence option B is the answer.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
